Feature: Toggle todo completion
  As a user
  I want to mark a todo as complete or active
  So that I can track my progress

  Background:
    Given the app is loaded

  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox marks a todo as completed
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
    Then todo "Buy milk" has the completed class

  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox again marks a completed todo as active
    Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
    Then todo "Buy milk" does not have the completed class

  Scenario: Mark all as complete toggles all todos
    Given a todo "First" exists
    And a todo "Second" exists
    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
    Then todo "First" has the completed class
    And todo "Second" has the completed class

  Scenario: Mark all as complete is checked when all todos are completed
    Given a completed todo "First" exists
    And a completed todo "Second" exists
    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked

  Scenario: Mark all as complete is unchecked when some todos are active
    Given a completed todo "First" exists
    And a todo "Second" exists
    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked

  Scenario: Unchecking mark-all unchecks all todos
    Given a completed todo "First" exists
    And a completed todo "Second" exists
    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
    Then todo "First" does not have the completed class
    And todo "Second" does not have the completed class
Feature: DOM node stability during state changes
  As a user
  I want my todo list to remain stable when I interact with it
  So that the interface stays responsive and predictable

  Background:
    Given the app is loaded

  Scenario: Toggling a todo preserves existing todo nodes in the DOM
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
    And the todo nodes are saved for identity check
    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
    Then todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
    And todo "Walk the dog" does not have the completed class
    And all todo nodes remain the same DOM objects

  Scenario: Toggling all preserves existing todo nodes in the DOM
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
    And the todo nodes are saved for identity check
    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
    Then todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
    And todo "Walk the dog" has the completed class
    And all todo nodes remain the same DOM objects
Feature: Remove a todo
  As a user
  I want to delete a todo I no longer need
  So that my list stays relevant

  Background:
    Given the app is loaded

  Scenario: Clicking destroy removes a todo
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
    When the user clicks the destroy button on todo "Buy milk"
    Then the todo list contains 1 item
    And todo "Buy milk" does not exist
    And todo "Walk the dog" exists
Feature: Clear completed todos
  As a user
  I want to remove all completed todos at once
  So that I can clean up my list quickly

  Background:
    Given the app is loaded

  Scenario: Clear completed removes all completed todos
    Given a completed todo "First" exists
    And a todo "Second" exists
    And a completed todo "Third" exists
    When the user clicks the clear-completed button
    Then the todo list contains 1 item
    And todo "Second" exists

  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when there are no completed todos
    Given a todo "First" exists
    Then the clear-completed button is hidden

  Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when there are completed todos
    Given a completed todo "First" exists
    Then the clear-completed button is visible
Feature: Active todo counter
  As a user
  I want to see how many todos are still active
  So that I know how much work remains

  Background:
    Given the app is loaded

  Scenario: Counter shows zero when no todos exist
    Then the counter shows "0 items left"

  Scenario: Counter shows the number of active todos
    Given a todo "First" exists
    And a completed todo "Second" exists
    Then the counter shows "1 item left"

  Scenario: Counter uses plural form for more than one active todo
    Given a todo "First" exists
    And a todo "Second" exists
    Then the counter shows "2 items left"

  Scenario: Counter updates when a todo is completed
    Given a todo "First" exists
    And a todo "Second" exists
    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "First"
    Then the counter shows "1 item left"

  Scenario: Counter updates when a todo is removed
    Given a todo "First" exists
    And a todo "Second" exists
    When the user clicks the destroy button on todo "First"
    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
Feature: Add a todo
  As a user
  I want to enter a new todo in the input field
  So that I can track something I need to do

  Background:
    Given the app is loaded

  Scenario: Creating a todo from a non-empty trimmed input
    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
    Then the todo list contains 1 item
    And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"
    And the new-todo input is empty

  Scenario: Trimming whitespace before creating a todo
    When the user types "  Buy milk  " into the new-todo input and presses Enter
    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"

  Scenario: Pressing Enter on an empty or whitespace-only input does nothing
    When the user types "" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
    Then the todo list contains 0 items
    When the user types "   " into the new-todo input and presses Enter
    Then the todo list contains 0 items

  Scenario: Multiple todos are appended in order
    When the user types "First" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
    And the user types "Second" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
    Then the todo list contains 2 items
    And the todo at position 1 has title "First"
    And the todo at position 2 has title "Second"
Feature: LocalStorage persistence
  As a user
  I want my todos to persist when I reload the page
  So that I do not lose my work

  Rule: Todos survive a page reload

    Scenario: Todos persist after reload
      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
      And a completed todo "Walk the dog" exists
      When the app is reloaded
      Then the todo list contains 2 items
      And todo "Buy milk" exists
      And todo "Walk the dog" exists
      And todo "Walk the dog" has the completed class

    Scenario: Editing persists after reload
      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
      When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
      And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and presses Enter
      And the app is reloaded
      Then todo "Buy oat milk" exists
      And todo "Buy milk" does not exist

    Scenario: Removal persists after reload
      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
      And a todo "Walk the dog" exists
      When the user clicks the destroy button on todo "Buy milk"
      And the app is reloaded
      Then the todo list contains 1 item
      And todo "Walk the dog" exists
Feature: Section visibility
  As a user
  I want the main section and footer hidden when there are no todos
  So that the interface stays clean

  Background:
    Given the app is loaded

  Scenario: Main and footer are hidden when there are no todos
    Then the main section is hidden
    And the footer is hidden

  Scenario: Main and footer appear when a todo is added
    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
    Then the main section is visible
    And the footer is visible

  Scenario: Main and footer hide when the last todo is removed
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user clicks the destroy button on todo "Buy milk"
    Then the main section is hidden
    And the footer is hidden
Feature: Edit a todo
  As a user
  I want to double-click a todo to edit its title
  So that I can correct or update what I need to do

  Background:
    Given the app is loaded

  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo activates editing mode
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
    Then todo "Buy milk" has the editing class
    And the edit input for todo "Buy milk" contains "Buy milk"
    And the edit input for todo "Buy milk" is focused

  Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edit
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
    And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and presses Enter
    Then todo "Buy oat milk" exists
    And todo "Buy milk" does not exist

  Scenario: Blurring the edit input saves the edit
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
    And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and blurs
    Then todo "Buy oat milk" exists

  Scenario: Trimming whitespace on save
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
    And the user types "  Buy oat milk  " in the edit input and presses Enter
    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy oat milk"

  Scenario: Saving an empty edit removes the todo
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
    And the user types "" in the edit input and presses Enter
    Then the todo list contains 0 items

  Scenario: Pressing Escape discards the edit
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
    And the user types "Changed" in the edit input and presses Escape
    Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk"

  Scenario: Editing mode hides the toggle and view controls
    Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
    Then todo "Buy milk" has the editing class
    And the toggle control for todo "Buy milk" is not visible
Feature: Hash-based routing
  As a user
  I want to filter my todos by All, Active, or Completed
  So that I can focus on the subset I care about

  Background:
    Given the app is loaded

  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
    Given a todo "Active" exists
    And a completed todo "Done" exists
    Then the selected filter is "All"
    And the todo list contains 2 items

  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
    Given a todo "Active" exists
    And a completed todo "Done" exists
    When the user navigates to "#/active"
    Then the selected filter is "Active"
    And the todo list contains 1 item
    And todo "Active" exists

  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
    Given a todo "Active" exists
    And a completed todo "Done" exists
    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
    Then the selected filter is "Completed"
    And the todo list contains 1 item
    And todo "Done" exists

  Scenario: Completing a todo hides it from the Active filter
    Given the user navigates to "#/active"
    And a todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
    Then the todo list contains 0 items

  Scenario: Uncompleting a todo hides it from the Completed filter
    Given the user navigates to "#/completed"
    And a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
    When the user toggles the checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
    Then the todo list contains 0 items

  Scenario: Active filter persists across reload
    Given a todo "Active" exists
    And a completed todo "Done" exists
    When the user navigates to "#/active"
    And the app is reloaded
    Then the selected filter is "Active"
    And the todo list contains 1 item
